    "rationale": "Evidence. The best raced design is iteration 7 (score 58.1734; oval 63.49, s-bend 66.85, slalom 44.19; no completions). Its sensors sit at y 0.08 m, span ±0.03 m, and use sensor_size 0.012, wheel_track 0.12, mass 0.8, kp 4.5, kd 0.1, base_speed 1.5. Every run still ends off_track with progress 0.11 to 0.16 and max_error 0.060 to 0.067. The 2-line-loss oval is the least-explained failure.\n\nWhat I accepted from the round-1 critique: (1) The draft's stated baseline was wrong. It attributed its gain to values never raced (kp 3.0, kd 1.0, wheel_track 0.14, mass 0.6, sensor_size 0.016). I reject that draft and restart from the raced iteration-7 design. (2) The draft's spacing change halved the signal slope per metre. Slope scales as weight step divided by spacing, so 0.33/0.01 = 33 per m becomes 0.33/0.02 = 16.7 per m. The critique is right that this silently halves steering gain. (3) kd 1.0 and above are unsupported. The derivative term is 100*kd per unit of signal change per step, and the earlier kd changes showed no clear damping effect. (4) The 18-point attribution to sensor y is wrong. Iteration 6 to 7 isolated the y change (0.06 to 0.08) and gained 0.38 points.\n\nWhat I kept: the core hypothesis that sensor reach limits the outer-offset readings, because the off-track excursions are where the array goes blind. I test it with a span change, not a y change, which the evidence has already shown is near saturation.\n\nWhat I changed: (a) Span widens from ±0.03 m to ±0.045 m, with 7 sensors at 0.015 m spacing (x = -0.045, -0.03, -0.015, 0, 0.015, 0.03, 0.045) at y 0.08 m. Spacing grows from 0.01 to 0.015 m, so the signal slope falls by a factor of 0.667. (b) To restore the raced steering gain, kp scales by 1/0.667 to 6.75, and kd scales the same way to 0.15, so the derivative-to-proportional ratio is unchanged. (c) sensor_size stays 0.012 m, so the 3 mm gap between footprints is the only new spacing effect, and the 12 mm footprint still covers the 25 mm tape edge at the outer offsets. (d) Everything else is held at the raced iteration-7 values (wheel_track 0.12, mass 0.8, base_speed 1.5, ki 0, line_loss 'last_direction').\n\nRisk: with kp 6.75, the outer wheel saturates near |signal| 0.36 instead of 0.65. In physical offset terms this is about 1.6 cm, close to the old 2.0 cm limit, but the margin is smaller on the sharpest bend. If the score falls below 58.17 or the oval max_error rises above 0.0652, the span change is the wrong lever and the next step is to revert to ±0.03 m and test sensor_size 0.016 at fixed span.\n\nFalsifiable targets versus 58.17: oval max_error below 0.06; line_loss_events at or below 1 on the oval and s-bend; slalom progress at or above 0.11; steering_oscillation not above 0.16. Expected result: a modest rise in progress on the s-bend and slalom. Completion is still unlikely at this base speed.",
